# Normalise line endings in the repository to LF.
#
# Without this file, `core.autocrlf=true` checks every file out with CRLF on
# Windows while the Prettier configuration requires LF, so every line of every
# file reports a lint error. Declaring the repository's own convention here
# takes the decision away from each developer's local git configuration.
#
# `text=auto` lets git detect text files and store them with LF, converting on
# checkout only where a platform needs it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Files that must never be line-ending converted.
#
# Luvax.html is a Claude Design export whose payload is base64 and gzip data
# embedded in the markup. Rewriting its line endings would corrupt the bundle.
docs/design/Luvax.html binary

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.eot binary
*.otf binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.mp4 binary
*.webm binary
